    "body": "Fixes #50623\n\n## Summary\n\nThe FULL cudagraph padding branches in the GDN attention metadata builder guard on `num_decodes`/`num_spec_decodes` but slice their preallocated buffers by `batch_size`:\n\n- **Spec-decode branch** (`vllm/v1/attention/backends/gdn_attn.py`): `batch_size` may include zero-length padded requests, so the guard does not bound the slice. A batch exceeding `decode_cudagraph_max_bs` would silently clamp the slice to the preallocated buffer length and downstream kernels would index a shorter tensor than the batch implies.\n- **Non-spec branch**: `batch_size == num_decodes` in a pure decode batch, so the guard does bound the slice — but this is not obvious from the code.\n\nThis PR adds `assert batch_size <= self.decode_cudagraph_max_bs` in both branches (as suggested by the reporter), making the invariant explicit and converting any future violation into a loud failure instead of silent misbehavior. No runtime behavior change in valid scenarios.\n\nAlso updates stale TODOs in `csrc/rocm/skinny_gemms.cu` per the issue's analysis: K % 8 is enforced by the call-site `TORCH_CHECK`, and the LDS-resident kernels are only dispatched when the activation fits in LDS (`WVSPLITK_CFG`), so the old \"64 KB\" and \"K multiple of 8\" warnings no longer describe the code. The file-level TODO's integer-overflow and stride notes are intentionally left untouched (stride fix pending in #50618; widening index math is a perf risk).\n\n## Why this is not duplicating an existing PR\n\nSearched open PRs referencing #50623 (0 results) and the GDN attention area: #45819 (batch invariance support) and #26807 (GatedDeltaNet APC) are unrelated. The issue has no assignee and no linked PRs; the reporter explicitly filed it \"rather than patching.\"\n\n## Test commands run and results\n\nNo runtime tests were run — the change is two always-true asserts plus comment-only edits, and the test environment was unavailable (torch not installed on the dev machine). Static verification:\n\n- `python -m py_compile vllm/v1/attention/backends/gdn_attn.py` — passed\n- `ruff check vllm/v1/attention/backends/gdn_attn.py` — all checks passed\n\nRelevant test to run in CI: `tests/v1/attention/test_gdn_metadata_builder.py` (CPU-only; its spec-decode cudagraph scenario uses `batch_size=2` vs `decode_cudagraph_max_bs >= 1024`, so the new asserts are trivially satisfied).\n\n## Model evaluation\n\nNot applicable — no change to model output, accuracy, or serving behavior (asserts only, always true under the existing invariant).\n\n## AI assistance\n\nThis PR was authored with AI assistance (opencode). The human submitter reviewed every changed line.",
